		<title type="html"><![CDATA[MD9600 Beta version is now available - including in Japanese]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2237&amp;p=18593#p18593"><![CDATA[
After a discussion with Colin G4EML, we've decided to call this latest version a Beta release<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/07cb014f0ec72c5a8c323f5ba0089e607d79dddc" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/07cb014f0ec72 ... 607d79dddc</a><br><br>No major changes from the last Alpha, except that Japanese versions are now available.<br><br>Note.<br><br>We are not close to have a full "Release" because at the moment, the current consumption when the radio is turned off, is still 100mA, which is far to high.<br><br>Colin did some tests and the official firmware consumes approximately 50mA when the radio is turned off. <br><br>However, I think this is much higher than is necessary, and I'm hoping to be able to get the "Off" current lower than the offical firmware. If possibly I want to get it to go much lower, but at the moment I don't know if thats practical.<br><br>Reducing the current when the radio is Off is not a trivial change to the firmware source code, so will NOT be available soon<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri May 20, 2022 6:47 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
